n":"Pittsburgh Steelers","abbreviation":"PIT","shortDisplayName":"Steelers","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-steelers"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/pit/pittsburgh-steelers"}}}}},{"id":2664,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:4","guid":"75b8623b-8926-b411-0476-3d3602b78523","description":"Cincinnati Bengals","sportId":28,"teamId":4,"team":{"id":4,"description":"Cincinnati Bengals","abbreviation":"CIN","shortDisplayName":"Bengals","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/cin/cincinnati-bengals"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/cin/cincinnati-bengals"}}}}},{"id":2203,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:2","guid":"232afaf2-01ac-fcc2-8bd6-66550df1703a","description":"Buffalo Bills","sportId":28,"teamId":2,"team":{"id":2,"description":"Buffalo Bills","abbreviation":"BUF","shortDisplayName":"Bills","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/buf/buffalo-bills"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/buf/buffalo-bills"}}}}},{"id":2610,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:24","guid":"84caf62b-c753-71ea-a787-44fd224a4294","description":"Los Angeles Chargers","sportId":28,"teamId":24,"team":{"id":24,"description":"Los Angeles Chargers","abbreviation":"LAC","shortDisplayName":"Chargers","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/lac/los-angeles-chargers"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/lac/los-angeles-chargers"}}}}},{"id":1979,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:1","guid":"49fd392a-86fe-4df3-1b77-9bbfa18b2ad5","description":"Atlanta Falcons","sportId":28,"teamId":1,"team":{"id":1,"description":"Atlanta Falcons","abbreviation":"ATL","shortDisplayName":"Falcons","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/atl/atlanta-falcons"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/atl/atlanta-falcons"}}}}},{"id":1861,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:9","guid":"06cd3bcf-7a86-53d4-28e7-aa049dd36261","description":"Green Bay Packers","sportId":28,"teamId":9,"team":{"id":9,"description":"Green Bay Packers","abbreviation":"GB","shortDisplayName":"Packers","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/gb/green-bay-packers"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/gb/green-bay-packers"}}}}},{"id":2830,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:33","guid":"38248455-3da4-84e4-8090-98b5cc38ffdc","description":"Baltimore Ravens","sportId":28,"teamId":33,"team":{"id":33,"description":"Baltimore Ravens","abbreviation":"BAL","shortDisplayName":"Ravens","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/bal/baltimore-ravens"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/bal/baltimore-ravens"}}}}},{"id":1298,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:6","guid":"b0fc8fb7-9dbe-e574-9008-6f0ee7c6b234","description":"Dallas Cowboys","sportId":28,"teamId":6,"team":{"id":6,"description":"Dallas Cowboys","abbreviation":"DAL","shortDisplayName":"Cowboys","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/dal/dallas-cowboys"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/dal/dallas-cowboys"}}}}},{"id":2553,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:13","guid":"b18540eb-6f2b-534c-e7f9-9bd930518da9","description":"Las Vegas Raiders","sportId":28,"teamId":13,"team":{"id":13,"description":"Las Vegas Raiders","abbreviation":"LV","shortDisplayName":"Raiders","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/lv/las-vegas-raiders"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/lv/las-vegas-raiders"}}}}},{"id":2035,"type":"team","uid":"s:20~l:28~t:18","guid":"97d2f6c9-2f22-459c-306a-046941ccab2a","description":"New Orleans Saints","sportId":28,"teamId":18,"team":{"id":18,"description":"New Orleans Saints","abbreviation":"NO","shortDisplayName":"Saints","links":{"mobile":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/no/new-orleans-saints"}},"web":{"teams":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/no/new-orleans-saints"}}}}},{"id":696224,"type":"contributor","guid":"a64fe5e2-0d9e-3aa3-8dd1-89b39e7d3d95","description":"Anthony Gharib","slug":"anthony-gharib","contributor":{"id":3959,"description":"Anthony Gharib"}}],"keywords":["NFL","Washington Commanders","Seattle Seahawks","Pittsburgh Steelers","Cincinnati Bengals","Buffalo Bills","Los Angeles Chargers","Atlanta Falcons","Green Bay Packers","Baltimore Ravens","Dallas Cowboys","Las Vegas Raiders","New Orleans Saints","Anthony Gharib"],"story":"<p><video1></p>\n<p>The long travel for an international game can make a victory even sweeter. In the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"38248455-3da4-84e4-8090-98b5cc38ffdc\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/bal/baltimore-ravens\">Baltimore Ravens</a>' case, it made the postgame troll just that much better.</p>\n<p><alsosee></p>\n<p>The Ravens defeated the <a data-clubhouse-guid=\"b0fc8fb7-9dbe-e574-9008-6f0ee7c6b234\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/team/_/name/dal/dallas-cowboys\">Dallas Cowboys</a> <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872960/ravens-cowboys\">34-31</a> in Rio de Janeiro following a last-second field goal by <a data-player-guid=\"16f0a87e-34cf-34ca-ad36-1c2245aa36e9\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4697745/tyler-loop\">Tyler Loop</a>. It marked the NFL's first game in Rio, and it surely lived up to the hype.</p>\n<p>With the score tied, Baltimore received the ball with seven seconds remaining. Ravens quarterback <a data-player-guid=\"7d76fbb1-1c5e-d9f4-954f-cad43f720ae2\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3916387/lamar-jackson\">Lamar Jackson</a> connected with wide receiver <a data-player-guid=\"04e6bfd5-ecba-2d02-bcac-087f32564877\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4429615/zay-flowers\">Zay Flowers</a> for 27 yards to set up a 56-yard boot from Loop. The kicker nailed it, giving Baltimore the win and a happy flight back home.</p>\n<p>On Wednesday, Jackson <a href=\"https://x.com/sportswcoleman/status/2102785745496748162?s=20\">was asked if he expected</a> the Cowboys to have a large contingent of fans in Rio since they are known as \"America's Team.\" The quarterback said, \"This is America, that's Brazil, so we'll see.\" The Ravens remembered the moment. They shared a video of running back <a data-player-guid=\"81c182a5-8981-2272-a00f-f8daf9533e07\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3043078/derrick-henry\">Derrick Henry</a> dashing past defenders toward his throne, while quipping that Baltimore is \"Rio's team now.\" Flowers <a href=\"https://x.com/ryanmink/status/2104365810794061846?s=20\">also said postgame</a>: \"We are Brazil's team.\"</p>\n<p><inline6></p>\n<p>Here are other top trolls from Week 3.</p>\n<p><img src=\"http://a.espncdn.com/i/infographics/20170710_nfl_fpr/charts/_end_rule.png\" width=\"100%\"></p>\n<h2><a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872950/bengals-steelers\">Pittsburgh Steelers 30, Cincinnati Bengals 27</a></h2>\n<p>An early-season AFC North clash predictably went down to the wire.</p>\n<p>Facing a three-point deficit with 2:15 left in the game, the Bengals received possession and started driving. They reached the Steelers' 38-yard line, but Pittsburgh defensive tackle <a data-player-guid=\"dda3e155-2461-3379-8a26-0218bf5962c7\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4682980/derrick-harmon\">Derrick Harmon</a> sacked quarterback <a data-player-guid=\"e6957db5-5b2e-a82d-c788-d889115d9772\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3915511/joe-burrow\">Joe Burrow</a>, resulting in a fumble the Steelers recovered to win.</p>\n<p>Ever the trollers, the Steelers wouldn't pass up on the opportunity to poke fun at their division rivals with cats being the theme. The Steelers posted a victory image with the caption: \"meoW,\" a video of a cat doing a viral dance and another cat photo captioned: \"raWr.\"</p>\n<p><inline2></p>\n<hr>\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872955/seahawks-commanders\">Washington Commanders 33, Seattle Seahawks 31</a></h2>\n<p>Washington defeated the Seahawks on Sunday, snapping Seattle's 13-game win streak. The Commanders entered the game with backup quarterback <a data-player-guid=\"33be1f4a-d812-75b9-7b7c-5319d2a7113a\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/2576980/marcus-mariota\">Marcus Mariota</a> under center due to <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4426348/jayden-daniels\">Jayden Daniels</a>' elbow injury.</p>\n<p>Mariota delivered by throwing for 183 yards and three touchdowns. Seahawks quarterback <a data-player-guid=\"938f19a1-ef9b-618c-2365-d55291e0fcc6\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/3912547/sam-darnold\">Sam Darnold</a> started for the first time since an oblique injury forced him out in Week 1. Darnold had 379 passing yards and four touchdowns but two interceptions -- the latter of which resulted in a pick-six with 3:57 left in the game.</p>\n<p>The Commanders went straight to trolling after the win. They shared a video from the hit comedy show \"The Office\" where Jim delivers coffee to Dwight, who can pick it up only with his toes and ends up spilling the hot drink on himself. In this case, Jim is the Commanders, delivering an \"L\" to Dwight, the Seahawks.</p>\n<p><inline1></p>\n<hr>\n<h2><a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872953/chargers-bills\">Buffalo Bills 24, Los Angeles Chargers 16</a></h2>\n<p>Buffalo stormed back to defeat Los Angeles and remain undefeated.</p>\n<p>The Bills began the fourth quarter down 13-10 and fumbled immediately. Chargers quarterback <a data-player-guid=\"ec880cbc-1490-cdae-548f-f844104974ae\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4038941/justin-herbert\">Justin Herbert</a> then threw an interception three plays later, which the Bills capitalized on by scoring a touchdown to go ahead for good. They iced the win with a final drive with 1:56 left in the game.</p>\n<p>Los Angeles is known for its elaborate social media posts when announcing its upcoming season's schedule. This year, it posted a <a href=\"https://x.com/chargers/status/2055068428978004027?s=20\">Halo-themed video</a>, which Buffalo referenced in its postgame jab.</p>\n<p><inline3></p>\n\n\n<hr>\n\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872961/raiders-saints\">Las Vegas Raiders 35, New Orleans Saints 27 </a></h2>\n\n\n<p>It's a 3-0 start for Las Vegas for the first time since 2021 following a road win against New Orleans.</p>\n<p>Las Vegas went ahead 35-27 with 6:22 remaining in the fourth then forced consecutive Saints fumbles to clinch its win. Raiders quarterback <a data-player-guid=\"53bec012-c2ed-bc7c-a8d5-438611f9faa1\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/14880/kirk-cousins\">Kirk Cousins</a> threw for 248 yards and three touchdowns, while tight end <a data-player-guid=\"bc4ba7ee-446b-36fd-9985-7fd2a94a98bc\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4432665/brock-bowers\">Brock Bowers</a> showed out in his season debut with 10 receptions for 116 yards and a score.</p>\n<p>While playing in the Big Easy, Las Vegas seemingly picked up on the region's dialect. The Raiders emphasized their 3-0 start in a postgame caption, spelling out \"Three & Eaux!\" in a reference to Louisiana Cajun culture.</p>\n<p><inline5></p>\n<hr>\n<h2><a href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/game/_/gameId/401872948/falcons-packers\">Atlanta Falcons 35, Green Bay Packers 14</a></h2>\n<p>Atlanta is a winner for the first time this season following an emphatic \"Thursday Night Football\" performance in Green Bay.</p>\n<p>The Falcons put up 498 yards of offense, outscoring the Packers 35-7 after falling behind 7-0 midway through the first quarter. In his first start of the season, Atlanta quarterback <a data-player-guid=\"28022fa1-9050-eee1-5160-c77a6a379ec2\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4360423/michael-penix-jr\">Michael Penix Jr</a>. threw for 256 yards and one touchdown, while running back <a data-player-guid=\"6667bcb0-dad1-3345-8e5a-a67ed4b010b0\" href=\"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4430807/bijan-robinson\">Bijan Robinson</a> had 213 total yards and two scores.</p>\n<p>The big victory came with multiple trolls aimed at the Packers, including a spin on the \"Go Pack Go\" chant and a reference to rapper T-Pain's \"Wiscansin\" lyric.</p>\n<p><inline4></p>\n\n\n\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"byline":"Anthony Gharib","isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50046373"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50046373"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/nfl/story?storyId=50046373"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50046373/nfl-week-3-trolls-2026"}},"premium":false}],"breakingNews":[],"timestamp":"2026-09-28T13:57:21Z","status":"success"}